WEBVTT

00:02.486 --> 00:04.745
        ♪<i> It seems today</i>
       <i> that all you see</i>
         ♪

00:04.821 --> 00:07.822
    ♪<i> Is violence in movies</i>
         <i> and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:07.824 --> 00:11.235
     ♪<i> But where are those</i>
   <i> good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.237 --> 00:14.329
 ♪<i> On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.406 --> 00:18.183
 ♪<i> Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.260 --> 00:21.353
   ♪<i> Lucky there's a man who</i>
       <i> positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.355 --> 00:22.929
♪<i> All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.006 --> 00:24.414
       ♪<i> Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.416 --> 00:30.070
          ♪<i> He's... a...</i>
       <i> Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:34.702 --> 00:38.278
Coming up tonight: Quahog's own
poet laureate comes to the set

00:38.355 --> 00:41.431
   and graces us with her...
   Oh, God, that's tonight?

00:41.433 --> 00:42.783
 Hey, Jerome, turn on the game.

00:42.859 --> 00:44.768
   Sorry, guys, cable's out.

00:44.770 --> 00:47.287
        We're only getting
        local stations.

00:47.364 --> 00:49.956
     Oh, what, so now we got
to talk sports to pass the time?

00:50.033 --> 00:52.626
 Or maybe watch<i> Gilmore Girls.</i>

00:52.702 --> 00:54.887
     Just as, like, a goof.

00:54.963 --> 00:56.797
           You know,
  if you want to talk sports,

00:56.873 --> 00:58.557
I've got quite a story to tell.

00:58.634 --> 01:01.376
    Oh! Oh! This is the one
   where Lorelai's mom makes

01:01.453 --> 01:03.453
   her martini with an onion
      instead of an olive.

01:03.455 --> 01:05.547
          Boy, that's
    a passive-aggressive move.

01:05.549 --> 01:07.641
      If you knew her mom,
       you'd know that's

01:07.717 --> 01:09.217
   a passive-aggressive move.

01:09.295 --> 01:11.236
          It all started
   when I was a young boy...

01:11.313 --> 01:13.772
          Last chance
  on this<i> Gilmore Girls</i> thing.

01:13.849 --> 01:15.890
   I was a baseball prodigy.

01:15.968 --> 01:17.743
        It was back home
      in the Cuban league.

01:17.745 --> 01:21.955
<i>I grew up working in the tobacco</i>
   <i> fields outside of Havana.</i>

01:21.990 --> 01:24.732
     <i> That's where I learned</i>
       <i> to play baseball.</i>

01:24.810 --> 01:28.403
<i> Our mitts were made of cigars,</i>
    <i> some of them still going.</i>

01:28.480 --> 01:31.648
          All right! Ha!
    All right, I caught it!

01:31.650 --> 01:34.501
   <i> At night I drove a cab.</i>

01:34.578 --> 01:37.487
       <i> We all had to drive</i>
         <i> huge cars there.</i>

01:37.489 --> 01:40.324
<i> I was just a regular young man</i>
          <i> wearing pants</i>

01:40.326 --> 01:41.767
<i>that went above my belly button.</i>

01:41.844 --> 01:44.019
       Pull your pants up.

01:46.498 --> 01:48.849
        <i> When I was nine,</i>
       <i> my father took me</i>

01:48.925 --> 01:51.501
   <i> to my first baseball game.</i>

01:51.503 --> 01:54.613
     <i> Fidel Castro was there</i>
 <i> to throw out the first pitch.</i>

01:54.615 --> 01:57.432
          <i> He was wearing</i>
    <i> the same outfit as always.</i>

01:57.434 --> 02:00.193
    <i> Later we would find out</i>
    <i> he had a fashion disease</i>

02:00.270 --> 02:03.013
            <i> known as</i>
    <i> Chronic Fatigue Syndrome.</i>

02:03.015 --> 02:05.124
    <i> We would write more jokes</i>
            <i> about him,</i>

02:05.200 --> 02:07.793
    <i> but our dumb-dumb writers</i>
 <i> only know what he looks like.</i>

02:07.870 --> 02:09.944
            Strike!

02:10.022 --> 02:12.047
    (cheering and applause)

02:13.634 --> 02:15.783
<i> We all worshipped Che Guevara.</i>

02:15.785 --> 02:18.620
<i>Although none of us really knew</i>
     <i> what side he was on.</i>

02:18.622 --> 02:19.713
           Thank you?

02:19.789 --> 02:22.290
     <i> But we knew he'd make</i>
          <i> a great poster</i>

02:22.292 --> 02:24.792
<i> in college dorm rooms someday.</i>

02:24.870 --> 02:28.129
     <i> ANNOUNCER: Please rise</i>
<i> for the Cuban National Anthem.</i>

02:28.207 --> 02:31.725
     (<i> I Love Lucy</i> theme song
             playing)

02:31.801 --> 02:35.379
       <i> CLEVELAND: In Cuba,</i>
    <i> we hated America so much,</i>

02:35.381 --> 02:37.322
<i> we copied everything they did.</i>

02:37.399 --> 02:39.974
<i> And died trying to get there.</i>

02:40.052 --> 02:42.077
  (crowd cheering, clamoring)

02:45.833 --> 02:47.057
          (music ends)

02:47.059 --> 02:49.168
   <i> Castro said there were CIA</i>

02:49.244 --> 02:52.396
     <i> all over our island,</i>
     <i> but I never saw any.</i>

02:52.398 --> 02:54.464
     (cheering, clamoring)

02:59.663 --> 03:02.255
    Yeah! Ha-ha! All right!

03:02.332 --> 03:06.185
     <i> But from that day on,</i>
 <i> I fell in love with baseball.</i>

03:06.261 --> 03:09.095
       <i> I dreamed of one day</i>
   <i> playing in the big leagues,</i>

03:09.097 --> 03:11.839
   <i> so I signed up for a montage</i>
          <i> to get better.</i>

03:11.917 --> 03:13.192
         (glass breaks)

03:13.268 --> 03:15.527
     (Cuban music playing)

03:23.687 --> 03:26.596
 <i> I was at the top of my game.</i>

03:26.598 --> 03:29.499
       <i> I didn't even need</i>
       <i> the full montage.</i>

03:31.286 --> 03:34.788
   <i> I was even recruited to play</i>
    <i> on Cuba's national team,</i>

03:34.864 --> 03:36.289
     <i> the Gooding Juniors.</i>

03:36.366 --> 03:38.775
       <i> ANNOUNCER: Tonight,</i>
    <i> the Cuba Gooding Juniors</i>

03:38.777 --> 03:41.478
<i>take on the Haiti Joel Osments!</i>

03:41.480 --> 03:43.630
       <i> We tried to play,</i>
       <i> but it was difficult</i>

03:43.632 --> 03:46.874
    <i> because hurricane season</i>
 <i> was February through January.</i>

03:46.876 --> 03:49.394
         (all shouting)

03:50.547 --> 03:52.973
    <i> Every time, a hurricane</i>
       <i> would sweep through,</i>

03:52.975 --> 03:54.975
     <i> decimating the island,</i>
         <i> causing hundreds</i>

03:54.977 --> 03:56.142
 <i> of dollars worth of damage.</i>

03:56.219 --> 03:57.461
              Aah!

03:57.463 --> 04:00.647
    <i> Under Castro, every male</i>
       <i> over the age of 18</i>

04:00.649 --> 04:04.034
     <i> was required to serve</i>
   <i> two years as a band leader.</i>

04:06.730 --> 04:10.415
       ♪<i> Babaloo-oo-oo</i> ♪

04:11.310 --> 04:14.828
       ♪<i> Babaloo-oo-oo</i> ♪

04:14.904 --> 04:17.422
           ♪<i> Jungo</i> ♪

04:17.499 --> 04:21.909
          ♪<i> Oo-oo-oo</i> ♪

04:21.987 --> 04:24.671
          ♪<i> Babaloo</i> ♪

04:24.748 --> 04:28.341
          (vocalizing)

04:28.418 --> 04:32.829
  ♪<i> Ta empezando lo velorio</i> ♪

04:32.831 --> 04:37.834
  ♪<i> Que le hacemo a babalu.</i> ♪

04:37.836 --> 04:41.446
       <i> I loved baseball,</i>
<i>but yearned to play in America.</i>

04:41.523 --> 04:44.524
 <i> I would look across the water</i>
         <i> and dream about</i>

04:44.601 --> 04:47.027
          <i> the great time</i>
    <i> they must be having there.</i>

04:47.029 --> 04:49.121
    I bet it's not so great.

04:49.197 --> 04:52.273
   ♪<i> If you're going my way</i> ♪

04:52.351 --> 04:55.352
      ♪<i> I want to drive it</i>
         <i> all night long</i> ♪

04:55.354 --> 04:58.463
    ♪<i> Oh, gimme, gimme, gimme,</i>
         <i> gimme, yeah...</i> ♪

04:58.465 --> 05:00.966
             Dang it!
   I'm at the wrong country.

05:00.968 --> 05:03.026
    <i> I knew what I had to do.</i>

05:03.028 --> 05:04.786
 <i> It was nothing against Cuba.</i>

05:04.863 --> 05:06.029
         <i> Cuba was nice.</i>

05:06.031 --> 05:07.547
    <i> We had a Bay of Hotties,</i>

05:07.624 --> 05:10.367
       <i> but also another bay</i>
    <i> of less attractive women.</i>

05:10.369 --> 05:12.627
<i> I forget what they called it.</i>

05:12.704 --> 05:15.480
    <i> However, tensions between</i>
   <i> the U.S. and Cuba were high.</i>

05:15.557 --> 05:18.375
     <i> Castro was not happy</i>
     <i> that they had named</i>

05:18.377 --> 05:21.803
 <i> the most dangerously gay part</i>
   <i> of San Francisco after him.</i>

05:21.805 --> 05:25.640
    <i> Defecting to the U.S. was</i>
<i> punishable by prison or death.</i>

05:25.717 --> 05:27.826
    <i> But I was determined.</i>

05:27.903 --> 05:29.386
     <i> Then came my chance.</i>

05:29.388 --> 05:31.054
 <i> The Cuba Gooding Juniors had</i>

05:31.056 --> 05:32.980
  <i> an away game in Barbados.</i>

05:33.058 --> 05:36.409
    Oy,    <i> herma</i> we can escape
     to the Cayman Islands.

05:36.486 --> 05:40.297
        Cayman, my ass.
     I'm going to America.

05:43.993 --> 05:45.993
 Okay, when we land in America,

05:45.995 --> 05:49.589
       we all have to stop
         saying "Cooba."

05:49.666 --> 05:53.243
       <i> The sea was choppy,</i>
<i>and the sharks were relentless.</i>

05:53.245 --> 05:54.911
           -(snores)
        -(knock on door)

05:54.913 --> 05:57.505
          -Who is it?
    -MALE: Uh, not a shark?

05:57.583 --> 05:59.599
        -Don't open it!
  -MALE: No, it's just people.

05:59.676 --> 06:01.434
     -MALE 2: Yeah, people.
      -MALE 3: And sharks.

06:01.436 --> 06:04.404
             MALE:
  Shh! No sharks. Just people.

06:08.369 --> 06:09.701
            <i> CLEVELAND:</i>
       <i> After a week at sea,</i>

06:09.703 --> 06:12.746
   <i> we saw the glittering lights</i>
            <i> of Miami.</i>

06:16.101 --> 06:17.859
           (cheering)

06:17.861 --> 06:19.694
      <i> It was beautiful.</i>

06:19.696 --> 06:21.955
         <i> Then we decided</i>
    <i> to go to Quahog instead,</i>

06:22.031 --> 06:23.548
<i> which took eight more months.</i>

06:23.625 --> 06:25.884
          <i> Eventually,</i>
     <i> I signed a large deal</i>

06:25.961 --> 06:28.278
 <i> with the Toronto Blue Jays.</i>

06:28.280 --> 06:30.204
       <i> But because I was</i>
   <i> from a warm-weather climate,</i>

06:30.282 --> 06:32.206
      <i> it didn't work out.</i>

06:33.560 --> 06:36.210
       <i> -I still remember</i>
   <i> my first major-league game.</i>
          -(cheering)

06:36.288 --> 06:39.456
       <i> It was four hours</i>
       <i> and 25 minutes long.</i>

06:39.458 --> 06:41.066
<i>I was like, "What the (bleep)?"</i>

06:46.815 --> 06:49.891
 Wow, Cleveland. I had no idea
      you played baseball.

06:49.968 --> 06:51.317
      Too bad you couldn't
          hit a home run

06:51.394 --> 06:52.469
    with<i> The Cleveland Show.</i>

06:52.471 --> 06:54.154
        Well, it certainly
        wasn't a whiff.

06:54.230 --> 06:55.488
       More of a foul out.

06:55.565 --> 06:57.416
        It was a double.

06:57.492 --> 06:58.992
           You know,
    you're not the only one

06:59.068 --> 07:00.735
who got a taste of sports glory.

07:00.737 --> 07:02.312
I had a pretty good run, myself.

07:02.314 --> 07:03.830
  Scrawny little guy like you,
           Quagmire?

07:03.907 --> 07:05.315
       What did you play?

07:05.317 --> 07:06.758
             I was
  a competitive tennis player.

07:06.835 --> 07:08.835
Some might say<i> too</i> competitive.

07:08.912 --> 07:10.837
           But I was
    the breath of fresh air

07:10.914 --> 07:13.339
  that the stuffy tennis world
            needed.

07:13.416 --> 07:15.750
            <i> I was born</i>
    <i> into a real tennis family.</i>

07:15.827 --> 07:18.595
     <i> On my first birthday,</i>
<i>my mother gave me a little Head.</i>

07:19.940 --> 07:23.333
    <i> I wanted to be the first</i>
   <i> male cheerleader for tennis.</i>

07:23.335 --> 07:26.260
   I cheer on two occasions:
          day and night!

07:26.262 --> 07:29.239
         -Ooh, tennis!
        -(crowd booing)

07:30.692 --> 07:34.453
    <i> And when that was weird,</i>
<i> I decided to just play tennis.</i>

07:36.848 --> 07:39.407
    <i> But it was understood I'd</i>
 <i> grow up to be a tennis player</i>

07:39.409 --> 07:41.685
          <i> like my father</i>
    <i> and his father before him</i>

07:41.687 --> 07:43.203
   <i> and his father before him.</i>

07:43.279 --> 07:45.797
    <i> We came from a long line</i>
         <i> of tennis dicks.</i>

07:45.799 --> 07:46.965
      <i> I had six brothers,</i>

07:46.967 --> 07:48.708
          <i> but they'd all</i>
     <i> sliced off their hands</i>

07:48.785 --> 07:50.284
   <i> opening a tennis ball can,</i>

07:50.286 --> 07:53.287
   <i> possibly the most dangerous</i>
    <i> object known to mankind.</i>

07:53.289 --> 07:55.882
           Hey, guys.
  Anyone want to play tennis?

07:55.959 --> 07:57.476
         Llewellyn, no!

07:58.628 --> 08:00.562
          (screaming)

08:03.650 --> 08:05.484
            <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
          <i> But I would do</i>
       <i> everything I could</i>

08:05.486 --> 08:07.819
            <i> to make</i>
   <i> my now-female father happy.</i>

08:07.896 --> 08:09.229
   <i> Practices were intense.</i>

08:09.231 --> 08:10.396
              <i> PETER:</i>
   <i> I feel like you skipped over</i>

08:10.473 --> 08:12.473
     <i> a very big story point</i>
          <i> right there.</i>

08:12.551 --> 08:14.384
            <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
          <i> My father was</i>
       <i> a World War II vet,</i>

08:14.386 --> 08:17.053
     <i> so he used to make me</i>
    <i> reenact the D-Day landing</i>

08:17.055 --> 08:18.404
   <i> with tennis ball machines.</i>

08:18.481 --> 08:19.664
            (gasps)

08:22.060 --> 08:23.668
           (grunting)

08:23.745 --> 08:25.562
    <i> But the work paid off.</i>

08:25.564 --> 08:27.488
          <i> I got invited</i>
    <i> to the first U.S. Open,</i>

08:27.566 --> 08:30.416
       <i> which, at the time,</i>
 <i> was called the U.S. Now Open.</i>

08:30.493 --> 08:33.512
    <i> There, I met the player</i>
<i> who would become my archrival:</i>

08:33.588 --> 08:35.680
    <i> Sweden's Hedd Banssen.</i>

08:36.908 --> 08:39.351
   <i> He'd bring his personal chef</i>
         <i> to every match,</i>

08:39.353 --> 08:40.744
 <i> which was very distracting.</i>

08:40.746 --> 08:42.187
               Aah!
          What the hell?

08:42.264 --> 08:44.672
  Hergy bergy meatball throwy!

08:44.750 --> 08:46.191
           (grunts)

08:46.268 --> 08:48.860
 Come on, this can't be legal.
      What are you, blind?

08:48.937 --> 08:51.363
          Serve ball!

08:54.183 --> 08:55.683
            <i> QUAGMIRE:</i>
   <i> I was the bad boy of tennis,</i>

08:55.761 --> 08:59.186
   <i> and my unconventional style</i>
    <i> of play changed the game.</i>

08:59.264 --> 09:01.540
     <i> Before I came along,</i>
     <i> tennis was so safe,</i>

09:01.616 --> 09:03.875
         <i> it was customary</i>
 <i> to hit a six-handed backhand.</i>

09:03.952 --> 09:07.212
          <i> I pioneered</i>
    <i> the one-handed backhand</i>

09:07.289 --> 09:10.382
         <i> and, eventually,</i>
    <i> the no-handed backhand.</i>

09:10.458 --> 09:11.699
           (cheering)

09:11.777 --> 09:14.611
Quagmire, I love your backhand.

09:14.613 --> 09:16.555
          That sounds
 like a backhanded compliment.

09:16.631 --> 09:17.872
        (audience gasps)

09:17.949 --> 09:20.541
<i>I also flouted tennis etiquette</i>

09:20.543 --> 09:22.561
            <i> by wearing</i>
   <i> the longest, baggiest shorts</i>

09:22.637 --> 09:24.971
   <i> the game had ever seen.</i>

09:24.973 --> 09:26.731
       <i> People criticized</i>
        <i> my style of play</i>

09:26.808 --> 09:28.975
<i> because I argued with umpires</i>

09:29.052 --> 09:30.960
          <i> and was taught</i>
   <i> to bounce the ball 40 times</i>

09:30.962 --> 09:33.029
       <i> before my serve.</i>

09:54.428 --> 09:55.635
           (grunts)

09:56.746 --> 09:58.972
             JUDGE:
       Let, first service.

10:10.685 --> 10:12.352
    <i> I'd won the U.S. Open,</i>

10:12.428 --> 10:14.187
     <i> but I wouldn't settle</i>
          <i> for just that.</i>

10:14.263 --> 10:17.282
            <i> My goal</i>
   <i> was the coveted Grand Slam:</i>

10:17.359 --> 10:20.860
    <i> pancakes, eggs, sausage</i>
     <i> and bacon at Denny's.</i>

10:20.937 --> 10:23.622
        One day, Glenn.
             One day.

10:23.624 --> 10:25.531
      Maybe your birthday.

10:25.608 --> 10:28.126
               ♪

10:32.691 --> 10:35.024
    <i> I made it to Wimbledon</i>

10:35.026 --> 10:37.284
         <i> and got to play</i>
    <i> in front of the queen--</i>

10:37.362 --> 10:38.544
       <i> Freddie Mercury.</i>

10:38.621 --> 10:41.622
<i> I altered my 40-bounce routine</i>
          <i> just for him.</i>

10:41.700 --> 10:44.017
     (bouncing and clapping
to rhythm of "We Will Rock You")

10:46.480 --> 10:50.373
    <i> It was an honor playing</i>
<i> for Freddie on grass that day.</i>

10:50.375 --> 10:53.559
         <i> He later died.</i>
<i>The doctor said it was asphalt.</i>

10:53.561 --> 10:55.111
              -♪
           -(grunts)

10:57.473 --> 10:58.615
           (grunting)

11:08.894 --> 11:10.585
           (cheering)

11:12.839 --> 11:16.341
 <i> It was the era before AIDS,</i>
 <i> but a lot of tennis players</i>

11:16.418 --> 11:19.419
   <i> had to deal with the scourge</i>
       <i> of Penis Gerulaitis.</i>

11:19.495 --> 11:21.404
       <i> Despite my on-court</i>
         <i> temper tantrums,</i>

11:21.406 --> 11:23.256
   <i> I was on top of the world.</i>

11:23.258 --> 11:26.351
    <i> And that's when I saw her:</i>
       <i> Tatum O'Seventies.</i>

11:26.428 --> 11:28.353
<i>The hottest actress of the era.</i>

11:28.430 --> 11:30.596
 <i> She was fresh off her success</i>
     <i> playing an 11-year-old</i>

11:30.673 --> 11:33.416
    <i> in a Little League movie,</i>
    <i> which, for some reason,</i>

11:33.418 --> 11:35.251
<i>made her the biggest sex symbol</i>
        <i> in Hollywood.</i>

11:36.196 --> 11:39.255
 -Thought you might need this.
      -Thanks. I'm Glenn.

11:39.257 --> 11:42.016
I know. I watched you smash your
  racket and scream at a baby.

11:42.093 --> 11:43.426
           You know,
    if you're free after this,

11:43.428 --> 11:45.019
  we could go back to my place

11:45.021 --> 11:47.597
   and try to fit some balls
           in your can.

11:47.599 --> 11:49.207
    <i> I practiced tantrum sex,</i>

11:49.209 --> 11:51.617
<i>something I'd learned from Sting</i>
    <i> but probably misheard.</i>

11:51.694 --> 11:54.771
           QUAGMIRE:
     What?! Are you crazy?
           That was in!

11:54.773 --> 11:58.365
<i>We became New York's "It" couple</i>
          <i> of the '70s.</i>

11:58.443 --> 12:01.202
  <i> We hung out at Studio 55.</i>

12:01.279 --> 12:03.221
   <i> There was no one there.</i>

12:03.223 --> 12:05.631
   <i> We could hear a lot of noise</i>
     <i> coming from next door.</i>

12:05.708 --> 12:09.619
   <i> I got to meet the greatest</i>
   <i> athletes of my generation.</i>

12:09.621 --> 12:11.804
   Glenn, how would you like
        to meet Bobby Orr?

12:11.881 --> 12:13.380
             -Or who?
          -Bobby Orr.

12:13.458 --> 12:15.382
       Yeah, Bobby or who?
     What's the other choice?

12:15.460 --> 12:17.477
        -It's Bobby Orr!
      -You told me Bobby's
       the first choice!

12:17.553 --> 12:19.720
    -What's the alternative?
    -All right, forget that.

12:19.798 --> 12:21.314
Do you want to meet Rick Monday?

12:21.390 --> 12:23.390
 Well, sure, I could do Monday,
          but who is it?

12:23.468 --> 12:26.661
         <i> By the 1980s,</i>
<i>things were starting to unravel.</i>

12:27.730 --> 12:28.821
            (yells)

12:28.898 --> 12:30.248
          Aw, damn it!

12:30.325 --> 12:32.584
     <i> My temper on the court</i>
    <i> was increasingly an issue.</i>

12:32.660 --> 12:33.810
              Out.

12:33.828 --> 12:36.312
       Are you serious?!
     You cannot be serious!

12:36.314 --> 12:39.257
       <i> I had a hard time</i>
<i>telling if people were serious.</i>

12:39.334 --> 12:41.242
     I spilled spot remover
           on my dog,

12:41.319 --> 12:42.761
       and now he's gone.

12:42.837 --> 12:44.411
           QUAGMIRE:
       Are you serious?!

12:44.413 --> 12:46.322
         <i> I became famous</i>
       <i> for smashing rackets</i>

12:46.324 --> 12:48.249
<i> when things didn't go my way.</i>

12:48.326 --> 12:50.251
     <i> Of course, back then,</i>
<i>we didn't have multiple rackets,</i>

12:50.328 --> 12:52.979
<i>so I was forced to play with it.</i>

12:55.850 --> 12:57.683
               ♪

12:57.760 --> 13:01.654
   <i> Ultimately, my career ended</i>
    <i> when I developed the yips.</i>

13:05.452 --> 13:09.436
<i> And in 2001, at the U.S. Open,</i>
   <i> my first serve hit a plane,</i>

13:09.514 --> 13:12.773
   <i> causing it to go tragically</i>
<i> off course and hit a building.</i>

13:12.851 --> 13:15.293
          (explosion)

13:15.370 --> 13:18.445
 <i> Everyone blamed the Muslims.</i>

13:18.523 --> 13:21.508
<i> My second serve was no better.</i>

13:29.868 --> 13:32.143
You guys talking sports stories?

13:32.220 --> 13:35.146
 You know, I won a bronze medal
      in the '84 Olympics.

13:35.223 --> 13:36.556
       Are you serious?!

13:36.632 --> 13:39.392
        Track and field.
   It's a pretty good story.

13:39.394 --> 13:41.986
 It's a series of coincidences
     that if someone wrote,

13:42.063 --> 13:44.471
     no one would believe.

13:44.549 --> 13:45.715
          (soft ding)

13:45.717 --> 13:48.217
          Oh, my God,
why is there only half a medal?

13:48.219 --> 13:50.644
               Hoo!
     How much time you got?

13:50.722 --> 13:52.572
  We got about seven minutes,
    and I haven't gone yet.

13:52.648 --> 13:53.890
            <i> Rocky.</i>

13:53.892 --> 13:55.725
               ♪

13:55.727 --> 13:58.911
    <i> Like most, my day began</i>
 <i> with block letters of my name</i>

13:58.988 --> 14:01.322
  <i> floating past the screen.</i>

14:01.399 --> 14:04.825
 <i> I grew up on the mean streets</i>
         <i> of Philadelphia,</i>

14:04.903 --> 14:06.660
 <i> the City of Brotherly Love.</i>

14:06.662 --> 14:09.663
 <i> Or, as I called it, America's</i>
    <i> Northernmost Hillbillies.</i>

14:09.741 --> 14:11.850
     <i> I was an Italian guy</i>
     <i> from the South Side</i>

14:11.926 --> 14:13.518
<i>who never had a chance in life.</i>

14:13.595 --> 14:17.597
 <i> But I had a dream: to one day</i>
    <i> be the heavyweight champ.</i>

14:17.673 --> 14:18.672
           Yo, Petey!

14:18.750 --> 14:19.691
           Yo, fella!

14:19.693 --> 14:21.359
           Yo, Petey!

14:21.436 --> 14:22.935
        Yo, Delayheehoo!

14:22.937 --> 14:24.253
      (lively harmonizing)

14:24.255 --> 14:26.255
       <i> It was a tough time</i>
         <i> in Philadelphia.</i>

14:26.257 --> 14:28.274
          <i> We were losing</i>
    <i> dozens of men every day</i>

14:28.351 --> 14:30.517
            <i> to singing</i>
    <i> over open trash can fires.</i>

14:30.595 --> 14:31.852
           Yo, Petey!

14:31.930 --> 14:33.020
        Yo, Flaming Guy!

14:33.022 --> 14:35.373
           Aah! Aah!

14:35.450 --> 14:38.359
<i>I was a two-bit knuckle breaker</i>
          <i> for the mob.</i>

14:38.436 --> 14:40.861
   <i> But it was a flash mob.</i>

14:40.863 --> 14:43.715
              -♪
     -You owe us two grand.

14:44.718 --> 14:46.551
    Don't make me come back.

14:46.628 --> 14:48.294
               ♪

14:48.371 --> 14:50.796
          You better pay
     or we'll funk you up.

14:50.873 --> 14:53.224
  I said we will funk you up.

14:53.301 --> 14:55.226
       <i> Like most fighters,</i>
          <i> I fell in love</i>

14:55.303 --> 14:58.212
 <i> with the local autistic girl</i>
 <i> who worked at the pet shop.</i>

14:58.289 --> 15:00.123
<i>I was one of her pet shop boys.</i>

15:00.125 --> 15:01.974
       Yo, hey, turtles.
          How you doin'?

15:02.051 --> 15:03.476
  How come they're not moving?

15:03.552 --> 15:05.478
    You sat on them yesterday.
         They're dead.

15:05.554 --> 15:08.722
   -What happened to your eye?
-I got beat up again in a fight.

15:08.724 --> 15:11.317
    Yo, Lois, the San Gennaro
    festival was last weekend.

15:11.319 --> 15:12.818
           You know,
    I was wondering if, uh,

15:12.895 --> 15:15.562
     -maybe you might want
      to go to it with me.
           -When is it?

15:15.640 --> 15:19.233
          -Last weekend.
   -Well, then I don't think
  that's possible, Peter. No.

15:19.310 --> 15:21.586
    <i> I could see she was gonna</i>
       <i> play hard to get.</i>

15:21.663 --> 15:24.405
    All right, okay, well, uh,
  want to maybe go to the park

15:24.482 --> 15:25.924
and feed the pigeons yesterday?

15:26.000 --> 15:28.593
      Peter, I already did
    yesterday stuff. Sorry.

15:28.670 --> 15:30.762
    Well, then how about we
  just get coffee this morning

15:30.764 --> 15:33.598
 -before you got to be at work?
  -It's 4:00 in the afternoon.

15:33.675 --> 15:35.841
           I'm afraid
 that's not gonna work, either.

15:35.843 --> 15:37.493
          Okay, well,
    I'll circle back last week

15:37.495 --> 15:39.253
           and see what
   your schedule looks like.

15:39.330 --> 15:42.774
 <i> I was not the smartest guy,</i>
 <i> but I wasn't gonna give up.</i>

15:42.850 --> 15:45.426
               ♪

15:45.503 --> 15:48.112
   <i> I lived in the Little Italy</i>
       <i> section of Philly.</i>

15:49.598 --> 15:52.525
    <i> My apartment was tiny.</i>

15:52.601 --> 15:54.694
           (grunting)

15:54.770 --> 15:58.531
    <i> I didn't have much stuff,</i>
   <i> but, still, it felt cramped.</i>

15:58.607 --> 16:00.274
          (clattering)

16:00.276 --> 16:03.294
<i>I really needed a bigger place.</i>

16:05.056 --> 16:06.297
<i>I wanted to work the speed bag,</i>

16:06.374 --> 16:08.374
    <i> but my gym was so cheap</i>
       <i> it didn't have one.</i>

16:08.451 --> 16:09.968
   <i> So I had to do the noises.</i>

16:09.970 --> 16:11.285
Dug-a-duh, dug-a-duh, dug-a-duh,
      dug-a-duh, dug-a-duh.

16:11.287 --> 16:12.470
          Harder hit!

16:12.472 --> 16:15.306
       <i> I fought my way up</i>
    <i> through the amateur ranks.</i>

16:15.383 --> 16:17.791
    <i> Most fights, my greatest</i>
<i>challenge was entering the ring</i>

16:17.869 --> 16:20.036
    <i> without getting completely</i>
     <i> tangled in the ropes.</i>

16:20.038 --> 16:22.371
           Little help?
        Is my butt out?

16:22.373 --> 16:23.481
    My butt's out, isn't it?

16:23.558 --> 16:25.817
   Sorry you got to see that
        back there, ma'am.

16:25.893 --> 16:28.319
     Yeah, I couldn't wipe.
  I had my gloves on already.

16:28.396 --> 16:31.397
 Stop taking pictures, please.

16:31.474 --> 16:34.400
<i>My least favorite part of boxing</i>
       <i> was the weigh-ins.</i>

16:34.477 --> 16:37.644
         -(snickering)
  -Hey, Keenan, Damon, Marlon.

16:37.722 --> 16:39.405
       Good luck, Peter.

16:39.482 --> 16:40.665
          (snickering)

16:40.742 --> 16:41.891
              Moo!

16:41.893 --> 16:43.559
          Oh, ha, ha.

16:43.561 --> 16:45.319
     <i> And I was the only guy</i>
          <i> who wouldn't</i>

16:45.396 --> 16:46.896
            <i> get naked</i>
       <i> in the locker room.</i>

16:46.898 --> 16:48.414
     I don't got a problem
          getting naked,

16:48.491 --> 16:51.567
          I-I just don't
   have to change right now.

16:51.569 --> 16:53.903
               ♪

16:53.905 --> 16:54.920
          <i> I became known</i>
       <i> as an up-and-comer</i>

16:54.997 --> 16:56.405
    <i> with a mean left hook,</i>

16:56.424 --> 16:59.350
     <i> who farted every time</i>
<i> he got punched in the stomach.</i>

16:59.427 --> 17:02.437
           (farting)

17:04.265 --> 17:07.266
    <i> By the second round, the</i>
<i> entire front row had pink eye.</i>

17:07.343 --> 17:10.269
   (punches landing, farting)

17:10.387 --> 17:12.271
       <i> I ran with a towel</i>
          <i> around my neck</i>

17:12.348 --> 17:14.273
    <i> tucked into my sweat suit,</i>
     <i> 'cause I always wanted</i>

17:14.350 --> 17:16.592
    <i> to look like a rich guy</i>
          <i> in a bathrobe.</i>

17:16.594 --> 17:19.445
     <i> Then I promised Lois</i>
<i>I'd see the Mark Rothko exhibit</i>

17:19.522 --> 17:21.614
       <i> at the Philadelphia</i>
          <i> Museum of Art.</i>

17:21.690 --> 17:24.450
     <i> But when I got there,</i>
          <i> it was closed.</i>

17:24.452 --> 17:26.419
               ♪

17:28.364 --> 17:30.864
    <i> Meanwhile, Lois and I</i>
    <i> were getting serious,</i>

17:30.942 --> 17:32.216
  <i> so I popped the question.</i>

17:32.293 --> 17:33.959
        Hey, listen, Lois,
        I was wondering,

17:33.961 --> 17:36.279
    if you're not too busy,
      what would you think

17:36.281 --> 17:38.539
about spending the previous part
      of your life with me?

17:38.616 --> 17:41.650
       I'm afraid that's
      not possible, Peter.

17:41.652 --> 17:43.619
        <i> But I was rising</i>
       <i> through the ranks</i>

17:43.621 --> 17:45.879
          <i> and fighting</i>
   <i> bigger and better opponents.</i>

17:45.881 --> 17:47.640
     <i> I fought Butterbean,</i>

17:47.716 --> 17:49.550
   <i> then I fought Can't Believe</i>
       <i> It's Not Butterbean.</i>

17:49.627 --> 17:52.386
       <i> I could barely tell</i>
         <i> the difference.</i>

17:52.463 --> 17:54.388
            <i> I fought</i>
    <i> Sugar Ray Leonard Nimoy,</i>

17:54.465 --> 17:56.482
            <i> who put</i>
   <i> a Vulcan nerve pinch on me.</i>

17:56.559 --> 17:58.484
       <i> The fight was deemed</i>
       <i> highly illogical.</i>

17:58.561 --> 18:00.986
            <i> I defeated</i>
    <i> Lennox Lewis and the News,</i>

18:01.063 --> 18:02.729
       <i> Evander Sallyfield</i>

18:02.731 --> 18:04.582
    <i> and Roberto Duran Duran.</i>

18:04.659 --> 18:06.309
          <i> I was supposed</i>
    <i> to fight George Foreman,</i>

18:06.311 --> 18:08.753
          <i> but I only got</i>
    <i> George ThreeMenAndaBaby.</i>

18:08.830 --> 18:10.571
    <i> There's a lot more puns,</i>
   <i> but this episode's only got</i>

18:10.648 --> 18:11.789
      <i> a few minutes left.</i>

18:11.866 --> 18:14.592
          <i> So finally,</i>
   <i> I got my shot at the title,</i>

18:14.669 --> 18:16.319
   <i> against a world champion--</i>

18:16.321 --> 18:18.988
<i> Marvelous Marvin Mrs. Maisel.</i>

18:18.990 --> 18:21.099
               ♪

18:22.418 --> 18:24.418
          Lois, no one's
     ever gone the distance

18:24.495 --> 18:26.345
     with Marvelous Marvin
      Mrs. Maisel before.

18:26.422 --> 18:28.681
       But if I can just
 get in that ring yesterday...

18:28.757 --> 18:31.517
           -Tomorrow.
   -and hear that bell ring,
        still standing,

18:31.594 --> 18:34.612
    I'll know I'm not just
    a bum from the streets.

18:34.614 --> 18:37.857
     I believe in you, Peter.
     Now go drink your eggs.

18:37.859 --> 18:40.676
               MAN:
    Aah! Our dinnerware hutch!

18:40.678 --> 18:42.436
            -Sorry.
        -(dish shatters)

18:42.513 --> 18:43.529
             Sorry!

18:43.606 --> 18:45.014
        Oh, they're mad.

18:45.016 --> 18:47.125
               ♪

18:50.279 --> 18:51.963
       <i> I was outmatched.</i>
          <i> A no-name punk</i>

18:51.965 --> 18:53.965
 <i> fighting the world champion.</i>

18:53.967 --> 18:56.283
     <i> I fought my heart out.</i>
       <i> I dug deep and had</i>

18:56.285 --> 18:58.452
   <i> a kick-ass song on my side,</i>
     <i> but we couldn't afford</i>

18:58.529 --> 19:01.288
    <i> the song from the movie,</i>
   <i> so we used the sound effects</i>

19:01.366 --> 19:02.306
   <i> from Nintendo </i> Punch-Out!!

19:02.642 --> 19:03.957
  -(video game music playing)
     -ANNOUNCER: Body blow.

19:04.035 --> 19:06.035
           Body blow.
      Body blow. Uppercut.

19:06.037 --> 19:08.295
 Uppercut. Body blow. Uppercut.

19:08.373 --> 19:10.723
          -(cheering)
        -(bell clanging)

19:10.799 --> 19:12.041
          -(grunting)
             -(clang)

19:12.043 --> 19:14.986
               ♪

19:17.398 --> 19:18.447
           (clanging)

19:19.550 --> 19:20.658
            (clang)

19:22.904 --> 19:24.829
         <i> The swollen eyes</i>
    <i> weren't from the fight.</i>

19:24.831 --> 19:26.906
 <i> There was a cat in the arena</i>

19:26.908 --> 19:29.016
   <i> -and I was highly allergic.</i>
             -(meows)
         -(bell dings)

19:29.093 --> 19:30.576
       <i> But I'd done it.</i>

19:30.578 --> 19:32.170
         <i> The only fighter</i>
    <i> ever to go the distance</i>

19:32.246 --> 19:33.078
       <i> with the champ.</i>

19:33.155 --> 19:34.154
      <i> But in that moment,</i>

19:34.415 --> 19:37.416
    <i> there was only one thing</i>
       <i> I could think about.</i>

19:37.493 --> 19:41.570
    Peter, the Rothko exhibit
    at the museum is reopened!

19:41.572 --> 19:43.664
    Are you busy last week?

19:43.741 --> 19:44.998
       <i> She had nailed me.</i>

19:45.000 --> 19:48.001
<i>I was, in fact, free last week.</i>

19:48.079 --> 19:50.930
<i>I was the pride of Philadelphia.</i>

19:51.006 --> 19:53.265
<i>Eventually, I became the champ.</i>

19:53.267 --> 19:55.526
          <i> I also changed</i>
     <i> my inspirational music</i>

19:55.603 --> 19:57.361
    <i> to keep me motivated.</i>

19:57.363 --> 19:59.588
         ♪<i> Baby shark,</i>
   <i> doo, doo, doo-doo, doo-doo</i> ♪

19:59.590 --> 20:01.699
    ♪<i> Baby shark, doo, doo,</i>
       <i> doo-doo, doo-doo</i> ♪

20:01.776 --> 20:03.926
         ♪<i> Baby shark,</i>
   <i> doo, doo, doo-doo, doo-doo</i> ♪

20:03.928 --> 20:05.761
        -♪<i> Baby shark...</i> ♪
             -Yeah!

20:05.763 --> 20:07.538
<i>Tragically, I died in training.</i>

20:07.615 --> 20:09.373
       <i> I fell into a vat</i>
   <i> of Philadelphia Cream Cheese</i>

20:09.450 --> 20:10.725
       <i> and suffocated.</i>

20:10.801 --> 20:12.618
          <i> I guess it</i> was
    <i> a little taste of heaven.</i>

20:12.695 --> 20:15.438
<i> Let's just say, at my funeral,</i>
    <i> there was quite a spread.</i>

20:15.440 --> 20:17.215
            <i> CLEVELAND:</i>
       <i> Some of this story</i>
    <i> ain't holding up for me.</i>

20:17.291 --> 20:18.624
              <i> PETER:</i>
         <i> I was cremated.</i>

20:18.701 --> 20:20.534
               <i> JOE:</i>
          <i> I don't think</i>
       <i> any of this is true.</i>

20:20.536 --> 20:22.637
              <i> PETER:</i>
       <i> My ashes were spread</i>
    <i> over an everything bagel.</i>

20:28.544 --> 20:30.786
   Hey, Joe, what about you?
 You're a pretty athletic guy.

20:30.788 --> 20:33.231
  -You got any sports stories?
     -Funny you should ask.

20:33.266 --> 20:34.640
    Actually, back in 1988,

20:34.642 --> 20:38.552
I took part in the Crystal Light
      Aerobics Competition.

20:38.629 --> 20:41.572
           ANNOUNCER:
    Representing Valley Health
     and Racket in Orlando,

20:41.649 --> 20:44.467
  Mona Hartnett, Debbie Harvey
     and Maressa MacEachin.

20:44.469 --> 20:45.726
               ♪

20:45.803 --> 20:48.153
     Representing Shofer's
    Athletic Club in San Jose,

20:48.230 --> 20:50.990
          Diane Terese,
Deborah McGee and Debbie Pardue.

20:51.066 --> 20:52.250
               ♪

20:52.326 --> 20:53.659
               <i> JOE:</i>
          <i> There I am!</i>

20:53.777 --> 20:54.977
 <i> That guy on the left's dead.</i>

20:54.979 --> 20:58.089
            <i> Asphalt.</i>